**Replace it entirely with this:**
```javascript
      {/* --- NEW CONFIRMATION MODAL --- */}
      <Dialog 
        open={isConfirmModalOpen} 
        onClose={() => !isSubmitting && setIsConfirmModalOpen(false)} 
        maxWidth="xs" 
        fullWidth
      >
        <DialogTitle sx={{ fontWeight: 'bold', color: 'primary.main' }}>
          Confirm Validation
        </DialogTitle>
        <DialogContent>
          <DialogContentText>
            You have successfully validated <strong>{rows.length}</strong> voucher entries. 
            <br /><br />
            <strong>Please note:</strong> You will not be able to modify these entries after proceeding to the next step. Are you sure you want to continue?
          </DialogContentText>
        </DialogContent>
        <DialogActions sx={{ p: 2, pt: 0 }}>
          <Button 
            onClick={() => setIsConfirmModalOpen(false)} 
            color="inherit" 
            disabled={isSubmitting}
          >
            Cancel
          </Button>
          <Button 
            onClick={handleConfirmSubmit} 
            variant="contained" 
            color="primary" 
            disabled={isSubmitting}
          >
            {isSubmitting ? <CircularProgress size={24} color="inherit" /> : "Proceed"}
          </Button>
        </DialogActions>
      </Dialog>

```
### What this does:
 1. **Clear Warning:** It tells the user exactly how many rows they have and explicitly warns them that modifications are locked out once they click Proceed.
 2. **Standardized Buttons:** Changes the secondary action to a standard "Cancel" button, which simply closes the popup and lets them continue editing if they realize they made a mistake.
 3. **Trigger Logic:** handleConfirmSubmit still fires correctly when "Proceed" is clicked, executing the database save and moving them to Step 3.
